    {
      "id": "image-title",
      "definition_id": "title-doc",
      "parameters": {
        "title": "Color Cardboard: multi-branch image processing"
      },
      "position": {
        "x": 686.6483961368176,
        "y": -421.48712738341993
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "image-instructions",
      "definition_id": "paragraph-doc",
      "parameters": {
        "text": "## Setup and run\n1. Choose **Demos → Add demo files to temporary user files**. Use the temporary folder, not a mounted directory.\n2. Click **Run workflow**. The input is the bundled ColorCardboard.jpg; no upload or external download is needed.\n3. Compare the color, grayscale, and rotated previews, then inspect the five metric values.\n4. Refresh User files and download Cardboard-color.png, Cardboard-gray.png, and Cardboard-rotated.png. Running again overwrites these generated files, not the original JPG.\n\nThis example uses existing Pillow and NumPy nodes; it does not require Fiji or ImageJ."
      },
      "position": {
        "x": 1185.9393119231493,
        "y": -420.93537142788256
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "prepare-notes",
      "definition_id": "paragraph-doc",
      "parameters": {
        "text": "## 1. Prepare a shared input\nRead the demo image, resize to 320 x 256 pixels, then crop the central region (left=32, top=32, right=288, bottom=224). Every branch starts from the same 256 x 192 crop. Resizing to a fixed size intentionally changes the original aspect ratio and keeps this demo lightweight."
      },
      "position": {
        "x": 1513.9850749226016,
        "y": -421.7643117965696
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "branch-notes",
      "definition_id": "paragraph-doc",
      "parameters": {
        "text": "## 2. Fan out into three branches\nColor: preserve the prepared RGB crop.\nGrayscale: convert to L mode.\nRotated: rotate the grayscale result 90 degrees with expansion enabled, producing 192 x 256 pixels.\nEach branch feeds both an inline preview and a lossless PNG export."
      },
      "position": {
        "x": 1868.1463494459351,
        "y": -420.3246389363376
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "metrics-notes",
      "definition_id": "paragraph-doc",
      "parameters": {
        "text": "## 3. Inspect image fluency\nThe grayscale crop also feeds Image Fluency Metrics. The five Show Value nodes display contrast, compression complexity, self-similarity, vertical symmetry, and horizontal symmetry (top to bottom). These are descriptive image measurements, not an overall quality score. Change the crop or source file and rerun to explore the differences."
      },
      "position": {
        "x": 2205.7510281979817,
        "y": -415.2122688760616
      }
    },
